# Text files are stored and checked out with LF on every OS: the code runs on Linux (Pi, Jetson), and a CRLF
# copy made on Windows breaks shell scripts (#!/bin/sh\r) and makes md5 checks against the robot fail.
# Folders with their own .gitattributes (hmc/docs/evidence/*: byte for byte) keep their rules.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.pdf binary
*.stl binary
*.onnx binary
*.engine binary
*.pt binary
*.pth binary
*.db binary
